{
  "about": "What a text becomes on the page. text is Markdown as an agent writes it; where is text, option-row (inside the label of a question's option) or option-detail (the expanded description, outside that label). form is strong, weak, copy-only or none. candidate is the written run the control covers, without backticks; for a link, its address. paths are what the page sends to GET /api/documents/resolve, without the suffix, the variant without a tail first. suffix is the anchor or line taken off. copy is what a click puts on the clipboard when the path cannot be opened; weak is never copied. caption is a link's text.",
